---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ownershipGuides } from "../data/ownership-guides";
import { comparisonGuides } from "../data/comparison-guides";
import { toThumbnail } from "../utils/images";

const [cars, problems, bestPages] = await Promise.all([
  getCollection("cars"),
  getCollection("problems"),
  getCollection("best")
]);

const flagshipCards = ownershipGuides.slice(0, 3).map((guide) => ({
  href: guide.href,
  title: guide.title,
  description: guide.description,
  eyebrow: guide.eyebrow,
  image: guide.image
}));

const comparisonCards = comparisonGuides.slice(0, 3).map((guide) => ({
  href: guide.href,
  title: guide.title,
  description: guide.description,
  eyebrow: guide.eyebrow,
  image: guide.image
}));

const snapshot = [
  { label: "Car hubs", value: cars.length },
  { label: "Problem guides", value: problems.length },
  { label: "Best-parts guides", value: bestPages.length },
  { label: "Ownership guides", value: ownershipGuides.length },
  { label: "Comparison guides", value: comparisonGuides.length },
  { label: "Strong clusters", value: 3 }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Updates"
  description="Recent updates to Kreativ Auto, including new ownership guides, better browsing, stronger fitment notes, and site-wide quality improvements."
>
  <div class="container-shell py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="surface hero-frame p-8 sm:p-10">
      <div class="grid gap-8 xl:grid-cols-[1.15fr_0.85fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Updates</p>
          <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">What changed and where the site is getting stronger</h1>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-steel">
            This page tracks the bigger editorial and structural improvements on Kreativ Auto, not every tiny patch. The goal is to make it obvious how the site is getting deeper, clearer, and more useful over time.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 text-steel">
            If you want the best current entry points, start with the flagship ownership guides, the comparison hub, and the stronger generation pages for Civic, RAV4, and Tiguan.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="accent-panel p-6">
          <p class="eyebrow">Current snapshot</p>
          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            {snapshot.map((item) => (
              <div class="soft-panel p-4">
                <p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">{item.value}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-steel">{item.label}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10 surface hero-frame p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="grid gap-8 xl:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Start Here</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Most important additions from the current site phase</h2>
          <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4">
            <div class="editorial-card">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Flagship guide layer</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
                The site now has real ownership guide coverage for the strongest clusters: common problems, maintenance costs and weak points, what to check before buying, what to avoid, and trim-buying guides.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="editorial-card">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Better browse flow</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
                Guides, best-parts pages, problem guides, and comparisons now have stronger hub pages, filters, and clearer internal paths instead of relying on flat listing pages alone.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="editorial-card">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Stronger commercial and editorial quality</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
                Core money pages now have tighter product links, clearer buying tiers, better imagery, and stronger quick-decision blocks. The strongest problem pages also have more useful first-check and stop-driving guidance.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid gap-4">
          <a class="mesh-card p-5 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5" href="/guides/">
            <p class="eyebrow">Flagship layer</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Open the guides hub</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">See the full ownership guide layer for the strongest clusters in one place.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="mesh-card p-5 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5" href="/comparisons/">
            <p class="eyebrow">Comparisons</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Open the comparisons hub</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Use drivetrain, engine, hybrid, and facelift comparisons where one symptom or one part page is too narrow.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="mesh-card p-5 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5" href="/generations/volkswagen-tiguan-tiguan-ii-facelift-2020-2024/">
            <p class="eyebrow">Generation hub</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">See the strongest generation example</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">The Tiguan II facelift hub is the clearest example of how the site now handles generation-level ownership guidance.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Flagship Guides</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Cornerstone pages added in the current phase</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
        {flagshipCards.map((card) => (
          <a class="overflow-hidden rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-white" href={card.href}>
            {card.image && (
              <div class="image-frame image-frame-card">
                <img
                  src={toThumbnail(card.image)}
                  alt={card.title}
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  width="960"
                  height="640"
                />
              </div>
            )}
            <div class="p-5">
              <p class="eyebrow">{card.eyebrow}</p>
              <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">{card.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">{card.description}</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Comparison Guides</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">High-value split guides added to the site</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
        {comparisonCards.map((card) => (
          <a class="mesh-card overflow-hidden p-0 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-white" href={card.href}>
            {card.image && (
              <div class="image-frame image-frame-card">
                <img
                  src={toThumbnail(card.image)}
                  alt={card.title}
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  width="960"
                  height="640"
                />
              </div>
            )}
            <div class="p-5">
              <p class="eyebrow">{card.eyebrow}</p>
              <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">{card.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">{card.description}</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6">
      <article class="surface p-6 sm:p-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">April 2026</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">From structured site to real editorial property</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-steel marker:text-accent">
          <li>Expanded the Civic, RAV4, and Tiguan clusters with more problem guides, more best-parts guides, and stronger internal linking between diagnosis, parts, and ownership pages.</li>
          <li>Built a real ownership-guide layer with common-problems, maintenance, pre-purchase, what-to-avoid, and trim-buying guides for the strongest three clusters.</li>
          <li>Turned the strongest generation pages into better starting points with common trouble spots, first parts to check, trim and year caveats, visual highlights, and clearer next-read paths.</li>
          <li>Moved comparisons into a dedicated public section, upgraded the comparison hub, and kept the old tools paths as redirects.</li>
          <li>Improved the strongest problem guides with quick verdicts, first checks, confusion points, and clearer signs that a car should not keep being driven.</li>
          <li>Improved the strongest best-parts pages with clearer buying tiers, stronger “best for” and “avoid if” logic, and tighter product-link quality.</li>
          <li>Added more branded and better-matched part imagery, generated thumbnails for faster browsing, and converted heavier hero images to lighter web formats.</li>
          <li>Improved the design system with stronger flagship-page treatment, denser image coverage, better typography, and more editorial hierarchy across the homepage, guides, and generation hubs.</li>
          <li>Added browse filters to the main hub pages so visitors can narrow the site faster by cluster, guide type, category, and symptom area.</li>
          <li>Refreshed trust pages, added a favicon, cleaned up public navigation, and kept the updates log aligned with the site’s stronger editorial direction.</li>
          <li>Added weekly and daily automation lanes so the site can keep drafting new content clusters and filling bounded content-quality gaps without hand-editing every pass.</li>
          <li>Added weekly and daily automation lanes so the site can keep drafting new content clusters and filling bounded content-quality gaps without hand-editing every pass.</li>
